# Case: Native Linux narrow window in dark appearance
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Inspect the real Linux skin, Chinese glyphs, search focus, menu and 600-point layout in dark appearance.
# Steps:
#   Open a 600x480 native Linux window; submit synthetic Chinese text; focus search through physical Ctrl+F; filter; open and dismiss the production command menu.
# Expected:
#   Chinese history and matching search remain accessible; the real command menu opens and Escape dismisses it; screenshots and native recording retain the actual composition.
# Forbidden:
#   IME claims from semantic field values, foreign skin overrides, software-view evidence or host clipboard access.

system-board-write 'UNIC-D Linux UI baseline'
start 600 480 dark
submit ui 'UNIC-D 原生中文布局验证'
ui-wait listItem 'UNIC-D 原生中文布局验证'
screenshot narrow-history
system-key Ctrl+F
ui-wait comboBox 搜索历史
ui-set comboBox 搜索历史 中文布局
ui-wait listItem 'UNIC-D 原生中文布局验证'
screenshot narrow-search
ui-set comboBox 搜索历史 ''
system-key Escape
system-key Escape
ui-click menuButton 更多操作
screenshot native-command-menu
system-key Escape
history-count 1
